# Rianell i18n conventions

## Key naming format

`{namespace}.{semantic.slug}` — always lowercase dot-separated words derived from English copy.

```json
// ✅ CORRECT
"wizard.saveEntry": "Save entry",
"settings.privacy.title": "Privacy & region",
"common.goals.setPrompt": "Set a goal"

// ❌ WRONG — no namespace, camelCase slug, or arbitrary keys
"saveEntry": "Save entry",
"privacyTitle": "Privacy & region"
```

## Namespace order (rollout sequence)

`common` → `nav` → `gate` → `consent` → `settings` → `wizard` → `logs` →
`modal` → `toast` → `charts` → `ai` → `export` → `tutorial` → `units` → `policy`

## Canonical source

- **`i18n-packs/locale-packs/v1/en-GB.json`** is the canonical source of truth
- Synced to apps via `scripts/i18n/sync-i18n-assets.mjs`
- Intentional English (brand names, medical codes like PHQ-2) → add to `scripts/.audit/i18n-allowlist.json`

## After any i18n change

```bash
npm run verify:i18n   # sync + locale/prompt/motd/HTML/audit + coverage --strict --max-pct=13
```

## MT / generation scripts

| Task | Script |
|------|--------|
| Generate Tier A overrides | `scripts/i18n/generate-locale-overrides.mjs` |
| Batch MT pass | `scripts/i18n/batch-mt-hybrid-keys.mjs` |
| Translate prompt packs | `scripts/i18n/translate-prompt-packs.mjs` |
| Verify mixed-language strings | `scripts/verify/verify-mixed-language-strings.mjs --locale=<lc>` |
